  "description": "A clip-on digital thermometer takes the mystery out of this no-bake classic.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: plain toasted sugar → lightly toasted sugar\n\nNotes: I love these cookies best with a blend of instant and old-fashioned oats, but it's fine to use just one or the other. Instant oats will produce a more homogeneous, cookie-like texture, while rolled oats will give them a heartier chew. You'll still be using a total of 85 g either way, but the volume will differ. For instant oats, use about 3/4 cup; for old-fashioned rolled oats (not thick-cut), use about 1 cup.",
